    "summary": "I couldn't build five drawers in one hex base. Instead the build is one north-half hex base with one drawer and solid end caps on its open edges. The checks pass and the parts don't collide.\n\n- **A full base takes no drawers.** A drawer only fits on the cut face of a half base. A half base has one cut face, so it takes one drawer.\n- **A quarter base takes none.**\n- **A 3-storey half base** gets more height, but it's really three bases stacked on top of each other, which goes against \"nothing on top\". I undid it.\n- **Notch and bay drawers** need two or three neighbouring bases, which goes against \"nothing beside\".\n\nIf you want more drawers, the closest options are a 3-storey half base, or a small cluster of bases with notch or bay drawers between them.",
